{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-329230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n| $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -2[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b \\\\ 4a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2a \\\\ -2b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-b+1 \\\\ 4a-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-b+1=-2a \\\\ 4a-2=-2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\nb=2a+1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n4a-2=-2(2a+1)\\,⇒\\,a=0.\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\nb=2(0)+1=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d99797b4f491521a6daa0960e51c902bba2bda06066a87ca134fa5d1c634572c"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{-2t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-329230" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$ where ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is sinusoidal. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d99797b4f491521a6daa0960e51c902bba2bda06066a87ca134fa5d1c634572c"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"] ["math" "{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d99797b4f491521a6daa0960e51c902bba2bda06066a87ca134fa5d1c634572c"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "{e}^{t}(t[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}])"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-332745" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-3t-4 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+4t+3\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot {e}^{2(0)} \\\\ {e}^{2(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot {0}^{2}-3\\cdot 0 \\\\ {0}^{2}+0+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}+1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-3 \\\\ {c}_{2}+1=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=-3.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}-3t \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d99797b4f491521a6daa0960e51c902bba2bda06066a87ca134fa5d1c634572c"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333613" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3=7 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=4.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]-5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d99797b4f491521a6daa0960e51c902bba2bda06066a87ca134fa5d1c634572c"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076563/state.json" "file_sha256" "8b63557ca0ad76710c59f15710e2b152abac428a68ec1d4819473086f5a5c359"} {"question" "q-333636" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refere